      {
        "id": 199256,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-07-03T23:23:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><b>MindWanderer wrote:</b></p>\n<div><blockquote>A team with more reliable ongoing control, more damage mitigation, and/or more damage output would do better. &nbsp;Swap GI Bunker for F6 Bunker, F6 Tempest for PW Tempest, and AZ for just about anyone with less setup (AZ can be great in this fight, but he's too random)&nbsp;and this would be more consistently winnable.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nEasy enough to try if you want. &nbsp;Let us know how you fare.&nbsp; \n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I forgot that GI was needed for the damage reduction, so I left him in. And I noticed that this was an entirely base-game team, so I left it at that. &nbsp;I chose vanilla Haka as an average character (i.e. not Legacy or F6/SS Tachyon) with no special advantage in this battle (unlike Ra and Vis).</p>\n<p>Experiment <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#1:</span> GI Bunker, PW Fanatic, PW Tempest, Haka. &nbsp;Except… by accident I chose Advanced instead of Challenge, but I didn't notice because I was using Bunker every round and fast-forwarding and only half paying attention to Blade's turns, so it was effectively Ultimate. &nbsp;Got Blade down into single digits, but did lose. &nbsp;Would have won handily without Advanced on.</p>\n<p>Experiment <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#2:</span> Retried the above game. &nbsp;Nearly identical result. &nbsp;This time noticed my error.</p>\n<p>Experiment <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#3:</span> Swapped PW Fanatic back for Redeemer and actually chose Challenge this time. &nbsp;PW Tempest never used his base power, and in fact F6 Tempest would have been better, since I had him skip a couple of turns to just draw more cards to try to deal with double Backlash Fields. &nbsp;Kraken was the MVP of this game: it heavily injured Tempest, then moved on to Blade. &nbsp;Fortunately, Fanatic got Zealous Offense right then and shut off the Kraken's damage until Blade was once again lowest. &nbsp;Tempest did get taken down by a couple of Slash &amp; Burns, but then used his incap power to double up on Krakens and bring Blade down that much faster.</p>\n<p>I could try again with vanilla Tachyon or Wraith, perhaps, but I'm convinced of my point. &nbsp;AZ is just not good–he's too setup-dependent, and even though he has ongoing control, he just has the one card and no way of getting to it faster. &nbsp;Wraith and Tachyon have even more ongoing destruction and damage mitigation, so they probably wouldn't have been any worse than Haka. &nbsp;There's certainly some luck, but I do think this becomes a much easier battle with a different team, namely, ditching AZ for someone faster and more consistent.</p>",
        "post_number": 32,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:27:19.658Z",
